<title>CHINA: China end-August forex reserves over $93 billion.</title>
<headline>China end-August forex reserves over $93 billion.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's foreign exchange reserves exceeded $93 billion at the end of August, central bank governor Dai Xianglong told an economic forum on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Vice Premier Zhu Rongji said reserves stood at $90.7 billion in early August.</p>
<p>Officials have said China's foreign exchange reserves could climb to nearly $100 billion by the end of this year.</p>
